[[!meta title="Energy Drink — Red Bull Winter Edition Pistachio & Berries"]]
[[!tag Energy_Drink Review]]

Red Bull released another Winter Edition on October 26 2026, which is two days
short of a year from [[last year's Winter
Edition|Red_Bull_Winter_Edition_Fuji_Apple_Ginger]]. It seems they release a new
seasonal editional every Winter, Spring and Summer these days. It's been that
way for a few years. It's funny that seasonal editions used to be rare and far
between. Nowadays you could use it as a proxy for the passage of time, like
watching the leaves fall or the sun drift West in the morning.

Anyway, like last year when I tried the Winter Edition, I'm a bit sick this year
as well, mostly owing to international travel. But even I can tell this year's
is good. We got a saying in this house:

<div>ANOTHER<br/>
RED<br/>
BULL<br/>
BANGER</div>

This was the first thing I thought of when I tasted Pistachio & Berries, this
year's Winter Edition.

<figure>
[[!template id="hooya-img.tmpl" cid="bafkreidu6jwmt3bj2faebpwqutmc2znhuymbjwpscyz3tsd6misjxzlgom" size=medium]]
</figure>

FUCK. It's good.

The first sip tastes like candy. Gummy candy, something that's got a bit of
citric acid but shows restarint that's rare in a candy. On the finish it's salty
and nutty. Which is a fascinating profile for a drink. The side of the can says
almost nothing about it other than:

> RED BULL® The Winter Edition, The Taste of Pistachio and Berries — artifically
> flavored. The Wings of Red Bull. Red Bull is appreciated worldwide by top
> athletes, busy professionals, college students and travelers on long journeys.

